{"max_tokens":16384,"messages":[{"content":"Infer the grid transformation using only explicitly observed outputs. Other public inputs have unknown outputs. Return eight self-contained Python 3.8 programs, each defining transform(grid) for ONE list-of-lists integer grid and returning one rectangular grid of colors 0..9, dimensions 1..30. Slots 0-1 implement p0, 2-3 p1, 4-5 p2, 6-7 p3, two plausible implementations per mechanism. Ordinary helper functions, loops and comprehensions are allowed. Only these modules may be imported: collections, functools, heapq, itertools, math. No file, network, process, clock or random access; no private attributes, dunder names, classes, decorators, async functions, dynamic eval or exec. Each program runs independently in a fresh bounded container on each input. Use ordinary safe builtins; no reflection. Type annotations are postponed. Keep each program within 8192 characters and 16384 UTF-8 bytes. Return code strings in hypotheses, without Markdown fences. Do not include task identifiers, reference solutions or other examples.","role":"system"},{"content":"{\"observations\": [{\"index\": 0, \"output\": [[9, 4, 9, 4, 4, 4], [9, 4, 4, 4, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 4, 9, 9], [4, 4, 4, 4, 9, 9], [9, 9, 4, 4, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 4, 4, 9]]}], \"plan\": {\"p0\": \"One possibility is to isolate the largest connected structure made of 4s, resample or pad it to 6\\u00d76, and use 9 for empty cells. The distinguishing assumption is that connectivity and component size determine which 4-pattern is retained; another input could select a different component or orientation.\", \"p1\": \"Another possibility is a fixed spatial projection from the large grid into a 6\\u00d76 grid: each output cell becomes 4 when its corresponding input region contains sufficient 4s, otherwise 9. This assumes location and regional density matter, not connectedness, so changing the placement of 4s could change the mask.\", \"p2\": \"A contrasting mechanism is to treat each non-9 color as a candidate layer, select color 4 because it is the relevant layer in the observed case, and copy its normalized six-by-six silhouette while suppressing colors 5 and 6. The distinguishing assumption is color identity rather than geometry; a different dominant color could be selected elsewhere.\", \"p3\": \"A further possibility is symbolic compression: the input contains several noisy colored motifs, and their relative arrangement is converted into a canonical 6\\u00d76 binary template, with 4 meaning a selected motif and 9 its complement. This assumes motifs are recognized by shape or role, so visually similar but differently colored motifs could yield different predictions.\"}, \"public_inputs\": [[[9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 4, 4, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 4], [5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 4, 4, 9, 4, 9, 4, 4, 4, 9, 4], [9, 5, 9, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 4, 4, 4, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 4, 9, 6, 6, 6], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 4, 4, 4, 4, 9, 6, 6, 6], [9, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 9, 9, 9, 4, 4, 9, 9, 6, 6], [9, 9, 6, 6, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 4, 4, 9, 6, 6], [6, 6, 6, 6, 9, 9, 9, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 6, 6], [9, 6, 9, 9, 9, 9, 5, 5, 9, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 6], [9, 9, 9, 9, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 6]], [[9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 3, 3, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 3, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 5], [3, 3, 3, 3, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 3, 3, 3, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 5, 9, 9], [9, 3, 3, 3, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 5, 5, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 5, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [4, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [4, 4, 4, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9